<title>USA: Ultramar talking to buy Total Petroleum-WSJ.</title>
<headline>Ultramar talking to buy Total Petroleum-WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ultramar Diamond Shamrock Corp is in talks to buy Total Petroleum (North America) in a deal worth more than $400 million plus debt assumption of $430 million, the Wall Street Journal said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ultramar Diamond, based in San Antonio, Texas, declined comment, and Total Petroleum told the paper it has discussed strategic alliances with Diamond Shamrock but that there is no offer on the table.</p>
<p>People familiar with the deal told the paper any offer would not carry a large premium over Total's current value.</p>
<p>Total closed Monday up 1/8 at 10-1/4. Ultramar Diamond closed up 5/8 at 29-5/8.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
